x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)=e^{3 x}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot y\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right) \\\\ \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\left(3\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot y & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x)):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\right) & =\\left(e^{3 x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495313 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\right)=\\left(e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(x e^{2 x^{2}}\\right)" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495313 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495313 1083 #uuid "06ad0058-543a-56f0-a30b-63445b19fb0b" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495314 1080 "\\frac{d}{dx}\\left(y\\cdot \\left(x\\right)\\right)=\\left(x\\right)\\cdot \\left(x^{2}\\right)" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495314 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495314 1083 #uuid "12a0cb4c-5470-5b60-b845-2fea9caa9516" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495315 1068 #edb/ref 17592186495325 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495315 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495315 1071 "Consider the following first-order linear ODE for the function $y = y(x)$:\n$\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=\\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}$\nWrite the equation in the form $\\frac{d}{dx}(yI(x)) = I(x)Q(x)$, where $I(x)$ is an integrating factor." 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495315 1072 #uuid "1fa0b599-1031-5002-a477-8a20611908f9" 13194139535322 17592186045443 true] [17592186495315 1074 